Connectome Canvas
=================

The code in this repository is MIT licensed — see LICENSE. That licence covers
the code and nothing else.

The connectome is not ours to license. The male Drosophila CNS connectome v1.0
is © HHMI Janelia FlyEM, the Cambridge Connectomics Group and Google Research,
released under CC-BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), and it
stays under CC-BY wherever it goes. `python run.py fetch` downloads it from the
public bucket gs://flyem-male-cns; nothing from it is redistributed here. If you
fork this, keep that attribution — it is the whole reason any of this is real.

The neuron model follows Shiu et al. 2024 (Nature) and the retinotopic drive is
argued for by Lappalainen et al. 2024 (Nature). Wiring this connectome to a
cursor through the descending neurons DNa02 / DNa01 / MDN / DNp09 was done first
and openly by the flybrain project (MIT); Connectome Canvas is an independent
implementation that points the same anatomy at a canvas.

Paintings produced by this software are hashed and, when minted, those hashes
and seeds are recorded on chain. Connectome Canvas is an art experiment, not an
investment, and nothing here is financial advice.
